      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before the Civil War, the town was called Calhoun's Landing, named after cotton planter Meredith Calhoun.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofcolfax.wixsite.com/colfaxlouisiana/about",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1873, the town witnessed a brutal Reconstruction‑era massacre that killed 150 African Americans and three whites, a pivotal event in civil rights history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colfax%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Red River Heritage Association, founded in 2007, collects and interprets Reconstruction history, especially in the Red River area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colfax%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A local nonprofit is raising funds to restore a historic bank near the courthouse into a museum, archives, and interpretive center.",
